   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Commonwealth Secretariat</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Political Engagement in Africa, Asia, Caribbean and the Americas, Europe, and the Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will adopt an evidence-based and data-driven approach to advance democratic resilience and other pillars of the Strategic Plan, driving inclusive participation and stronger institutions to enhance the Secretariat&#x2019;s visibility. This will be achieved by adopting a more responsive approach and leveraging the Commonwealth&apos;s trusted partnerships with governments, civil society, including youth and women, and access to political stakeholders and leaders. The regional sections will work with regional organisations such as AU, ASEAN, CARICOM, PIFs, UN, and others, including NGOs and the private sector leaders. The regional sections will conduct ongoing and systematic political analysis of global and regional political developments including early situational awareness, advising the Secretary-General and her envoys, as well as technical teams, supporting the adherence to Commonwealth values in each region, fostering democratic processes, and peaceful conflict resolution. This approach will enhance the Secretariat&apos;s visibility and responsiveness in safeguarding the provision of consensus building forums and supporting states in a coordinated role.</narrative>
  </description>
